   ans:"<b>Decompensated liver cirrhosis due to HBeAg-negative chronic hepatitis B</b> (HBV DNA 25,000 IU/mL) — <b>Child-Pugh class B (9 points)</b>: bilirubin 2.4 (2), albumin 2.8 (2), INR 1.5 (1), moderate ascites (3), no encephalopathy (1) · <b>MELD ≈ 14</b> (MELD-Na ≈ 18–19) — <b>with portal hypertension</b> (SAAG 2.8 − 0.6 = <b>2.2 g/dL</b>, splenomegaly, <b>hypersplenism</b>: WBC 3,900, platelet 82,000) <b>and moderate (grade 2) ascites without SBP</b> (PMN 36/mm³) · mild hyponatremia (Na 132) · mild anemia · ไม่พบ HCC (US ไม่มีก้อน, AFP ปกติ)",
